## Metal–Organic Frameworks
Formation of a Syndiotactic Organic Polymer Inside a MOF by $[2+2]$ PhotoPolymerization Reaction
Pedaling for cylobutane polymers: A syndiotactic polymer ligand embedded inside a metal–organic framework (MOF)
was formed through pedal motions of spacer ligands before undergoing a $[2+2]$ cycloaddition reaction in the solid state.
